\f0\fs24 \cf2 Welcome to the Red Room, the bedroom of Giuseppe Bagatti Valsecchi and Carolina Borromeo. Here, time seems to have stopped: the original arrangement has been faithfully preserved, just as we see it in historical photographs. Every piece of furniture, every detail is in its place. Only the original upholstery, once rich and sumptuous, has been lost. But there\'92s another element that deserves our attention: the chandelier. It\'92s not just a decorative object, but a creation based on the original design of the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers. The inspiration? An altarpiece from the early 16th century, painted by Gandolfino da Roreto for the Cathedral of Asti, depicting the Marriage of the Virgin. This is a perfect example of how the two brothers didn\'92t just collect, but creatively reinterpreted Renaissance models, adapting them to the style of their home. A chandelier that not only lights up the room, but tells a story of love for art and the past.\
}